  body: "# Category D Retirement Pension: age and residence boundary\n\n## Source-backed proposal\n\nThe chapter’s
    Category D provision is non-contributory but specifies pensionable-age timing, age 80, other Retirement Pension
    entitlement and residence conditions.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nAge 80 alone does not establish Category
    D entitlement. The GB residence and ordinary-residence requirements, disregarded components and international
    chapter references need separate review. Entitlement displaced by overlapping-benefit rules is not automatically
    absent.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 75221, PDF page 56](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=56).\n\
    - [DMG 75227, PDF page 58](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=58).\n\
    \n## Provenance and review\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of DWP guidance, not an official DWP document.
    All definitions and relationships are model-assisted and unreviewed. No individual eligibility, award, legal
    conclusion or executable rule is supplied.\n\nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, stated
    legal date and pension event date have separate meanings. PDF page numbers are one-based file positions; extraction
    may damage reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n-
    `dmg-vol12-ch75` — PDF SHA-256 `655e7acb31f09f5169efbe40419091ee479f88c0c45b65c7a507b042b67712f9`; page-extraction
    SHA-256 `0d037880d2aeaff1be89235ee987ca4acb1c839fcf1ead8b8be2daa9f6795465`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-overlapping-benefits
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source treats certain RP entitlement as existing despite non-payment under
      overlapping-benefit provisions when considering Category D.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch75/0058
      quote: "75227 People are treated as entitled to RP if they would be entitled but for the overlapping benefit\n\
        provisions. Therefore, people will not be entitled to a Cat D RP if their entitlement to another Cat RP
        is\nhigher than the weekly rate of Cat D but is not payable."
      locator: DMG 75227
